.TH ADI2-EQ 1 "November 2026" "rme-adi2-control 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
adi2-eq \- turn an ADI-2 EQ profile into a SysEx message
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adi2-eq
.RI [ profile.json ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-binary ]
.RB [ \-\-send ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.IR model ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B adi2-eq
builds the SysEx block that applies an EQ profile to an RME ADI-2 unit.
Without a profile it uses the bundled Beyerdynamic DT 1990 Pro profile. The
message is printed as hex unless written to a file or sent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-output " file
Write the SysEx message to
.IR file .
.TP
.B \-\-binary
Write raw bytes (a .syx file) instead of hex.
.TP
.B \-\-send
Send the message to the unit with
.BR amidi (1).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
ALSA raw MIDI port, for example hw:3,0,0. Detected automatically by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " model"
Target model:
.B dac
(the default),
.B pro
or
.BR pro24 .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adi2-control (1),
.BR amidi (1)
